traceability.evidence:
Story file exists and defines detailed requirements:
- docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md includes acceptance criteria for JSDoc coexistence, termination, boundary detection, continuation logic, error messages, backward compatibility, documentation, and tests.

Implementation:
- Core behavior is implemented in src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts:
  - processCommentLine includes explicit JSDoc coexistence handling:
    ```ts
    // Implement JSDoc tag coexistence behavior: terminate @story/@req values when a new non-traceability JSDoc tag line (e.g., @param, @returns) is encountered.
    // @supports docs/stories/022.0-DEV-JSDOC-COEXISTENCE.story.md REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC
    if (isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized)) {
      finalizePendingAnnotation(context, comment, options, pending);
      return null;
    }

    if (pending) {
      const continuation = normalized.trim();
      if (!continuation) {
        return pending;
      }
      const updatedValue = pending.value
        ? `${pending.value} ${continuation}`
        : continuation;
      return {
        ...pending,
        value: updatedValue,
        hasValue: pending.hasValue || continuation.length > 0,
      };
    }
    ```
  - This ensures: non-traceability JSDoc tags terminate current annotation values (REQ-ANNOTATION-TERMINATION, REQ-CONTINUATION-LOGIC), while true continuation lines (not starting with a JSDoc tag) are concatenated.

- JSDoc tag boundary detection utility in src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts:
  ```ts
  /**
   * Detect whether a normalized comment line starts with a non-traceability JSDoc tag.
   * ...
   * Related requirements:
   * - REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION
   * - REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE
   */
  export function isNonTraceabilityJSDocTagLine(normalized: string): boolean {
    const trimmed = normalized.trimStart();
    if (!trimmed || !trimmed.startsWith("@")) {
      return false;
    }

    if (/^@(story|req|supports)\b/.test(trimmed)) {
      return false;
    }

    return true;
  }
  ```
- This matches the story’s required pattern `/^\s*\*?\s*@\w+/` and treats any `@word` that is not @story/@req/@supports as a boundary, fulfilling REQ-JSDOC-BOUNDARY-DETECTION and REQ-JSDOC-TAG-COEXISTENCE.

